V4L2 UAPI headers

linux/videodev2.h, linux/v4l2-controls.h and linux/v4l2-common.h are verbatim
copies from Linux 6.12 (include/uapi/linux). Each carries
"(GPL-2.0+ WITH Linux-syscall-note) OR BSD-3-Clause" and is used here under
the BSD-3-Clause option.

linux/media.h is written for FreeBSD from the documented interface (struct
layouts, ioctl numbers, constant values), BSD-2-Clause. It is not derived from
Linux's media.h, which is GPL-2.0 only; tests/abi compares every constant, every
struct size and every ioctl against that header, read from a Linux tree.

linux/v4l2-subdev.h, linux/v4l2-mediabus.h and linux/media-bus-format.h are
GPL-2.0 only and are deliberately NOT copied; the same replacement is still to
be done for them (open question Q1 in docs/specs/SPEC_media_v4l2_native.md in
bzdOS/bsdOS).
